                <pb facs="0759" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.51/174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-05-04T22:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1921—10
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 5—9:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>37. President appears consider business needs of the country oblige him transfer
                    gold reserve in New York to London. Says would be glad if Lima banks permit him
                    to transfer in New York £4,000,000 gold now held inactive here [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">there</hi>].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
